    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-bb9a62c93992\",\"class\":\"expressible\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"domain-no-infra-import\",\"type\":\"forbiddenDependency\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"to\":\"module:src/infra/**\",\"scopePaths\":[\"src/domain/**\"]},{\"id\":\"domain-no-infra-require\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"pattern\":\"require\\\\(\\\\s*['\\\"][^'\\\"]*infra\",\"path\":\"src/domain/**\"}],\"coverage\":\"Every import edge (import, import type, export-from, import()) from a src/domain module to any src/infra module in the post-change tree. Unresolvable imports in src/domain also fail. CommonJS require() calls naming an infra path are caught as well.\",\"residual\":null,\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/domain/leak.ts b/src/domain/leak.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/leak.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+import { pool } from '../infra/db/pool';\\n+export const p = pool;\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/domain/leak2.ts b/src/domain/leak2.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/leak2.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+const m = require('../infra/db/pool');\\n+export const p = m;\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/domain/extra.ts b/src/domain/extra.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/extra.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\\n+export const extra = 1;\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"The rule is a pure module-graph prohibition. A forbiddenDependency on src/domain/** → src/infra/** decides it directly on the post-change tree, including type and dynamic imports. A line pattern covers require() calls, which the graph may not model. No meaning or intent is involved.\"}",
